    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="1359" n="1245" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> J.C.S. Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d589-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C.C.S. 255/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-03">3 September 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Operations of Red Air Force Subsequent to</hi> “<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Tidalwave</hi>”</p>
                <p>In C.C.S. 255<anchor n="2" xml:id="d589-f2"/> the U.S. Chiefs of Staff suggested
                    that the Combined Chiefs of Staff recommend to the President and Prime Minister
                    that <pb facs="1360" n="1246" xml:id="pg1246"/> at the proper time, subsequent
                    to <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tidalwave</hi>, they jointly request Premier
                    Stalin to have the Russian Air Force undertake a folloW–up mission against the
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tidalwave</hi> objective.</p>
                <p>At their 98th Meeting on the 18th of June, it was noted that the proposal
                    contained in C.C.S. 255 had been submitted to the British Chiefs of Staff, from
                    whom a reply had not yet been received. It was further noted that the British
                    Chiefs of Staff would be informed that the proposal was not intended to be
                    presented to the President and Prime Minister until after <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Tidalwave</hi> had been accomplished.</p>
                <p>Now that <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tidalwave</hi> has been accomplished,<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d589-f3"/> the United States Chiefs of Staff wish to renew the
                    proposal contained in C.C.S. 255 and recommend that immediate action be taken
                    with a view to implementing this proposal.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d589-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d589-f1-content">
                <p>For the action taken on this paper at the 117th and 118th Meetings of the
                    Combined Chiefs of Staff, September 3 and 10, 1943, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1206">pp. 1206</ref>, <ref target="#pg1225"
                        >1225</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d589-f2" n="2" xml:id="d589-f2-content">
                <p>“Operations of Red Air Force Subsequent to ‘<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Soapsuds</hi>’ “, June 15, 1943; not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d589-f3" n="3" xml:id="d589-f3-content">
                <p>Concerning the air attack of August 1, 1943, against the Ploeşti oil facilities,
                    see Dugan and Stewart, <hi rendition="#italic">Ploesti</hi>, chapters 6–11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
